{
  "suite": "pace_im",
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "description": "PACE Integrated Mapping: implemented for all eight IM OIDs, where upstream's doPACEStep2IM is an explicit stub that throws after MSE:AT + the step-1 nonce exchange already hit the chip. The suite pins the OID dispatch, the two typo'd protocol OID names, and both App H value chains end to end: the P11 §4.4.3.3.2 pseudo-random mapping R_p(s,t), f_G via the App B.2 affine point encoding (H.1, Brainpool P-256) and f_g = x^((p-1)/q) (H.2, RFC 5114 1024/160), each followed by the key agreement, session keys and both authentication tokens. Reject rows cover the p != 3 mod 4 guard (NIST P-224), the P11 §4.4.3.3.2 MUST ĝ != 1, and the App B domain limits. App H publishes only AES-128 chains; 3DES, AES-192 (the truncation note), AES-256 and the other groups/curves are python-oracle rows generated by conformance/tools/pace_mapping_oracle.py, lower assurance, and labelled as such. The upstream stub throw stays pinned in transcripts/pace_session_im_partial.json (swift-only).",
  "runners": [
    "dart",
    "swift"
  ],
  "cases": [
